 r←RefreshData opt;build_opt;new;result;⍙CACHE;cache_file;tie
⍝ opt: whether to build cache in isolate or main process :: Boolean
⍝   r: when the cache rebuild completed, for interactive callers :: simple character vector
 :Trap 202 404
     ##.IMPORT.YOUTUBE.RefreshData''
 :Else
     ##.Log'[REFRESH] DATA NOT REFRESHED. ',⎕DMX.Message
 :EndTrap
 build_opt←(
     using:##.⎕USING
     app_dir:##.app_dir
 )
 :If opt
     ⍙CACHE←#.ø #.DCMS.CACHE         ⍝ Spawn isolate to build cache in separate process
     result←⍙CACHE.Build build_opt   ⍝ Build new cache in isolate. Does not block threads in main process despite waiting for future to resolve.
     ##.Log'[REFRESH] ⍙CACHE isolate running:',#.isolate.Running'result'
     'new'⎕NS result                 ⍝ Must deep clone 'new'⎕NS ref because result ref from namespace-returning isolate cannot be dotted into (interpreter bug)
 :Else
     'new'⎕NS #.DCMS.CACHE.Build build_opt
 :EndIf
⍝ Must deep clone any sub-namespaces of cache to make cache self-contained and serialisable
 new.presenters←⎕NS¨new.presenters
 new.events.data←⎕NS¨new.events.data
 new.videos←⎕NS new.videos

⍝ Write out newly created cache to file, so a future deployment can instantly pick up
⍝ the built cache and start serving responses.
 cache_file←##.GetEnv'CACHE_FILE'
 :Trap 11 20 24   ⍝ Namespace not self-contained
     :If ⎕NEXISTS cache_file
         tie←cache_file ⎕FTIE 0
         new ⎕FREPLACE tie 1
     :Else
         tie←cache_file ⎕FCREATE 0
         new ⎕FAPPEND tie
     :EndIf
 :Case 11
     ⎕←'Could not write ',cache_file,'. New cache namespace is new self-contained.'
 :Case 20
     ⎕←'Could not write ',cache_file,'. File exists but component was not created.'
 :Case 24
     ⎕←'Could not write ',cache_file,'. File already tied.'
 :EndTrap
 ⎕FUNTIE tie

 new.videos.(index←1500⌶index)   ⍝ Prime index for hashing
 new.videos.(Lookup←index∘⍳)     ⍝ Create index function
 {}new.videos.(Lookup 1⌷index)   ⍝ First use of lookup function causes hash to build

 #.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache←new         ⍝ Single-line update is safe across threads. Readers take snapshots to get complete cache view.

 ##.Log'[REFRESH] ',r←'Refreshed #.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache'
